SELECT '3079710f-a2bc-4e9d-a72a-69ba41722966', ct.id, $ctx$Roys and Rep. Lisa Subeck announced the Abortion Rights Restoration Act (LRB-2921) on April 23, 2025, which would eliminate Wisconsin's 1849 near-total abortion ban along with waiting periods, ultrasound requirements, provider limitations, telehealth restrictions, admitting-privileges rules, and the release's "Coverage bans" item — the statutory bar on abortion coverage in public-employee health plans and in qualified health plans offered through the state ACA exchange. (CORRECTED ON REVIEW: an earlier draft of this reasoning said the bill repeals a bar on *Medicaid* coverage; the source release does not mention Medicaid. Verified against the release text 2026-07-27.) Removing access restrictions plus the coverage prohibition matches chair 1's compound "legal, accessible, and publicly funded at all stages." NOTE FOR REVIEWERS: the "publicly funded" clause is satisfied here by repeal of a prohibition on publicly-funded-plan coverage, not by an affirmative appropriation. She and Subeck reintroduced a similar Abortion Accessibility Act on Oct. 1, 2025, showing a sustained rather than one-off position.$ctx$,
