SELECT '79744617-8efa-439f-86fe-b13c253c6cdb', ct.id, $ctx$In a 2025-08-22 statement Udell opposed ending no-excuse mail-in voting after Trump floated the idea, warning it would disenfranchise elderly, disabled, military, and student voters. In a 2026-03-19 statement he opposed the federal SAVE Act's added voter-registration documentation requirements, specifically defending Wisconsin's existing mail-in and online voter-registration options and citing Kansas data on wrongful-rejection rates under similar documentation rules. Both statements affirmatively defend no-excuse mail-in access rather than merely opposing strict photo ID, matching chair 2's 'expand early voting periods and make mail-in voting available to all voters without requiring an excuse' rather than the ID-focused chairs 3-5.$ctx$,
